tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:5: //! (PR-5) and this round's own doc,
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:6: //! docs/planning/green-program/failure-capture/PR-5-2026-09-06.md.
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:7: //!
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:8: //! Three things are checked here, deliberately kept apart:
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:9: //!
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:10: //! 1. Census-anchored wiring: each gate script that sources the drain lib
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:11: //!    (not a literal list of four names -- the file set as it exists on
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:12: //!    disk) calls both `gcd_drain_and_report` and `gcd_pass_report`
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:13: //!    somewhere in its body.
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:14: //! 2. The actual ratchet: each "guest kill" line in a converted gate --
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:15: //!    `kill $QEMU_PID`/`kill "$QEMU_PID"`/`kill $RUNNER_PID`/`kill
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:16: //!    "$RUNNER_PID"`, each followed by `2>/dev/null`, the one shape each
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:17: //!    outcome-kill in these four scripts uses -- has a drain-decision call
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:18: //!    within the KILL_WINDOW lines immediately before it. A mutation test
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:19: //!    proves this actually reddens: relocating a real kill line to sit
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:20: //!    ABOVE its drain-decision block (literally "move the kill above the
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:21: //!    drain") makes the check fail where the unmutated file passes.
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:22: //! 3. A functional oracle over the shell library itself, run with no QEMU
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:23: //!    boot: the SAME ordered capture starts with BEGIN and one event. A
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:24: //!    controlled wait writes the remaining event and END synchronously.
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:25: //!    Disabled draining reads partial before that transition; enabled
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:26: //!    draining crosses it and reads complete using the real classifier.
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:27: //!
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:28: //! # Why line-window text matching, not an AST
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:29: //!
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:30: //! These are bash scripts. A window-based textual check cannot see through
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:31: //! an indirection (a kill issued from a variable holding a function name,
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:32: //! say), the same limitation `capture_path_lock_free_structure.rs`'s own
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:33: //! denylist documents for its source scan. What it catches -- the actual
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:34: //! shape each kill site in these four scripts uses today, verified by the
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:35: //! census below finding six of them -- is what this PR shipped, and the
tests/gate_capture_drain_structure.rs:36: //! mutation test proves the check is not vacuous against that shape.
