docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:388: # executes at all and this pin would be vacuous. `selection_capped` is the
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:389: # production selection cap firing; its exact value is a property of how many
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:390: # receipts happened to be ready per pass rather than of the claim, so it is
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:391: # shape-pinned rather than value-pinned.
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:392: #
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:393: # The four `pend_*` fields attribute the settled queue depth term by term, using
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:394: # the same lock-free predicate the drain uses to choose a receipt.
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:395: # `pend_selectable=0` is the load-bearing one: a receipt the drain could have
