docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:418: UDP_PORTS_LOCK_ORACLE_LITERAL='[UDP_PORTS_LOCK_ORACLE:x86:arm=none:reason=uniprocessor_no_udp_ports_contention_peer:online_cpus=1:SKIP]'
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:419: # #821. Unlike the two SKIPs above, this oracle has a real arm on x86: the
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:420: # defect it measures is worse here than on aarch64, because `manager()`
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:421: # performs no mask operation on this architecture, so the boot thread's
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:422: # driver-test window holds PROCESS_MANAGER with IF=1 and an input interrupt
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:423: # taken on top of it, on a machine that boots -smp 1, would wait for a lock its
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:424: # own CPU owns.
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:425: #
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:426: # `pm_blocking_acquires=0` is the property: a production counter that each of
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:427: # the 3 blocking PROCESS_MANAGER accessors bumps while the input IRQ entry's
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:428: # no-blocking scope is open. `fg_unset_before=1` is the precondition, since the
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:429: # deferring branch is only live while no foreground pgrp is set.
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:430: # `pm_held_during_entry=1` and `irqs_enabled_before=1` are the pair that says
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:431: # the injection really ran under a held, unmasked lock -- and on this
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:432: # uniprocessor profile the entry's mere completion under that hold is the
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:433: # reading, which is why the trailing arm is pinned to `local_hold`. The oracle
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:434: # reports `handler_would_block` and refuses to drive that injection when its
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:435: # own detector says the entry still reaches a blocking acquisition, so the
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:436: # unrepaired kernel reddens this gate instead of hanging the boot.
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:437: #
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:438: # `entry_us` is deliberately pinned loosely here: this profile's monotonic
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:439: # clock is TSC-backed only when the TSC is calibrated, and a millisecond-
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:440: # resolution fallback would make a tight pin a flake rather than a reading.
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:441: # The aarch64 gate carries the timed reading; this one carries the
docker/qemu/run-x86-boot-tests.sh:442: # completed-under-hold reading.
